# BOHEMIA SIDE QUEST — PLAYABLE .bq (canon machine layer)
# S04 — WHAT CRIES IN THE DEEP
# Shape: contract / the-monster-is-a-person (Witcher). Faction wires: HOMELESS,
# NETWORK. This is the one in the batch that BRUSHES the secret (contrast makes it
# land): the "haunt" screaming in the deep tunnel at night is a neurolinked person
# half-taken by the network, grieving, stranded near the water where the deep runs
# down. Root the monster in a wronged human (W7): investigate and the sanctioned
# kill reframes as mercy or rescue, never scored. Amalgamation canon respected —
# the danger is PROXIMITY to the secret, not the creature's strength; going loud
# down there is what draws the wrong attention. No proper names (W8). CLOUT rides
# the deed: lead them out gently -> #quiet; put them down loud for the bounty ->
# #reckless; seal the tunnel and lie that it is gone -> #risky.

# ---- QUESTBOOK STUDY CITATIONS (QUEST STUDY LAW, 7/26/26) -------------------
# The corpus this quest is actually built from. Every id below resolves in
# records/BOHEMIA_QUESTBOOK_LAW_INDEX.json (3,672 citable findings mined out of
# the 152 studied quests in questbook/), and gates/quest_study_gate.js verifies
# the id AND the quoted law title verbatim. A citation is a claim the machine
# can check, never a name-drop.
# @STUDY Q004.W6  THE AMBIGUOUS PETITIONER
#   applied: the haunt is a grieving neurolinked person and a genuine danger at the same time; you cannot resolve it into one thing.
# @STUDY Q001.W11  NO CLEAN WIN
#   applied: mercy, rescue and bounty all cost something real; none of them is the clean read.
# @STUDY Q021.W2  "YOU CAN'T SAVE EVERYONE" AS THE THESIS
#   applied: the deep is where you learn you were never going to save everyone down there.
# @STUDY Q022.P7  W9 (sympathy for the enemy
#   applied: the thing in the deep is humanized until putting it down costs the player something, which is the whole reason the bounty framing hurts.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

@QUEST   bq_deep_cry   What Cries in the Deep
@ACT     2
@FACTION NONE
@ONCE    true

@ROLE elder     REQ  faction=HOMELESS  keeps_the_tunnel=true
@ROLE haunt     REQ  neurolinked=true  grieving=true

@STAGE 10
  @LOG The tunnel elders will pay to end the crying that comes up the deep every night.
  @DO show_objective 10
@STAGE 20 #namedbody
  @LOG It isn't a haunt. It's a person, half-taken, sitting where the deep runs down toward the water.
  @DO show_objective 20
  @DO complete_objective 10
@STAGE 30 COMPLETE #quiet
  @LOG Talked them up out of the deep, slow, in the dark, one word at a time. They walked out on their own feet.
  @DO bond haunt +25
  @DO faction HOMELESS +6
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 31 COMPLETE #reckless
  @LOG Ended it loud in the deep, for the bounty. The crying stopped. Something far below noticed the noise.
  @DO faction HOMELESS +8
  @DO set_flag looked_under_the_rock
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 32 COMPLETE #risky
  @LOG Sealed the deep tunnel and told the elders it's gone. It isn't gone. It's just quieter now, and walled in.
  @DO faction HOMELESS +6
  @DO set_flag walled_them_in
  @DO complete_objective 20
@STAGE 33 FAIL #quiet
  @LOG Couldn't do any of it. Left the crying where it was. The elders will find someone with a harder stomach.

@OBJ 10  "Find the source of the crying"   target=elder
@OBJ 20  "Decide what the crying is"        target=haunt

@TALK hire  speaker=elder  entry=stage>=10
  @SAY Every night it comes up the deep. Crying. Sometimes words, and the words are worse than the crying. #dread
  @SAY The little ones can't sleep. We don't go down that far. You aren't one of us, so you can.
  @SAY End it. I don't care how. I care that it stops. Don't tell me how.
  @OPT "I'll go down and look."         [gate: none]  -> descend  @DO learn going_deep
  @OPT "What's down the deep?"           [gate: none]  -> what
  @OPT "Find someone else."               [gate: none]  -> refuse
  @NOVERB "Promise it is gone for good"
@END

@TALK what  speaker=elder
  @SAY Water. Old pipe. And below that, further than anyone sane goes, more water and a hum you feel in your teeth. #dread
  @SAY We don't ask about the hum. We ask about the crying. Go find the crying.
  @OPT "Going down."                      [gate: none]  -> descend  @DO learn going_deep
@END

@TALK refuse  speaker=elder
  @SAY Then you're no use to me and my back hurts from this conversation. #tired
  @OPT "Sorry."                           [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 33
  @OPT "No, wait. I'll go."             [gate: none]  -> descend  @DO learn going_deep
@END

# THE DESCENT. The reveal must be found by walking into it, not in an optional
# node (W3): stepping onto stage 20 IS the reveal, and stage 20 is unavoidable.
@TALK descend  speaker=haunt  entry=stage>=10 and knows:going_deep
  @SAY don't shine that at me. i know what i look like now. i know. #dread
  @SAY they took the half of me that could go home. the other half stayed down here where it's cool and it remembers her.
  @SAY you have a stick or a wire or a bounty. i can hear it in how you breathe. so do it, or don't, but stop breathing at me.
  @DO set_stage 20
  @OPT "Nobody is doing anything. Talk to me."   [gate: none]  -> talk_up
  @OPT "The elders paid me to end this."          [gate: none]  -> honest
  @OPT (lower the light, sit down)                [gate: none]  SILENCE -> talk_up
  @NOVERB "Ask what the network took"
@END

@TALK honest  speaker=haunt
  @SAY of course they did. I'd pay too, if it cried under my children. #dread
  @SAY so here is the whole menu. lead me out, which is slow and i might not make it. end me, which is fast and loud and you shouldn't be loud down here. or wall me off and lie, which is the coward's mercy and it works.
  @OPT "Come up. Slow. I've got you."     [gate: none]  -> lead_out
  @OPT "I'm sorry. I'll make it quick."  [gate: none]  -> end_it
  @OPT "I'll seal it and say it's gone."  [gate: none]  TRAP -> wall_it
@END

@TALK talk_up  speaker=haunt
  @SAY you're still here. people aren't usually still here. #hope
  @SAY there's a way up if a person walks it with me and doesn't let go and doesn't get loud. loud is bad down here. loud is very bad. can you be quiet and stubborn at the same time.
  @OPT "Come up. Slow. I've got you."     [gate: none]  -> lead_out
  @OPT "I can't. I'm sorry."              [gate: none]  -> end_it
  @OPT (take their hand)                    [gate: none]  SILENCE -> lead_out
@END

@TALK lead_out  speaker=haunt
  @SAY one word at a time. don't look down at the water. look at me. keep looking at me. #hope
  @SAY there. there's the air. i forgot the air moved. thank you for being quiet. thank you for being stubborn.
  @OPT "You walked it yourself."           [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 30
@END

@TALK end_it  speaker=haunt
  @SAY okay. okay. do it up here where it isn't so dark, if you can, and be quick, and please don't be loud about it after. #dread
  @OPT "Look away. It's over."            [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 31
  @OPT (do it without a word)              [gate: none]  SILENCE -> END  @DO set_stage 31
@END

@TALK wall_it  speaker=haunt
  @SAY the wall. the coward's mercy. it works, you know. it actually works. #dread
  @SAY they'll sleep. I'll be quieter. everybody gets a little of what they wanted and nobody has to look at me. go on. build it.
  @OPT "Sleep now. Nobody will look."      [gate: none]  -> END  @DO set_stage 32
@END
